{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-ir.5.1:000028:note_appended:bob-cli-ir.5.1.3:067ab36df332fb6accfe5f6f12f80ed228ebe23d23a379764f094f069f776243","timestamp":"2026-11-09T02:47:32Z","actor":"bob-cli-ir.5.1.3","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-ir.5.1.3","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"JSON/contract for bob-cli-ir.5.1.4 and bob-cli-ir.11: capture success adds top-level note_files (skip_serializing_if empty) with path, action=\"create\", record_type, properties[{key,label,value,display,source}], body, markdown. Item record_note is serde skip and collected into note_files. value/display are Option<String> (display copied into value so CaptureResult stays Eq; choice displays use labels like \"Liked\"). source is \"typed\"|\"default\". Dry-run and commit share exact markdown bytes. Incomplete records exit 2 with extra.draft (ready-to-copy, title @dir/ or @dir/^stem, typed fields, omitted required as key:: … plus choice/date hints), extra.missing, extra.invalid[{field,code,message}]. Collisions use code record_exists and copy \"record already exists: {path} (open it; adding to it with `@{dir}/{stem}` comes later)\". schema_version stays 1; GRAMMAR_REVISION stays 20. No new capture subcommand or public flag. Planner: capture/record_note.rs stages via CaptureBatchPlanner with target_existed false; reserved_paths from planner.staged_snapshot() (records, projects, templates). Missing parent dirs created only at commit (ensure_new_file_parents) and rolled back when empty; PLANT_BEFORE_INSTALL race keeps foreign bytes. Human dry-run: \"{prefix} would create  {ordinal}{emoji}new {kind}  {target}\"; then exact markdown. Success: \"{prefix} {emoji}new {kind}  {ordinal}{target}\" plus field displays and \"{n} note(s)\". Record items skip Gmail rewrite, task-block, freshness, ledger, relations."}}
